<SimpleContentLayout
  eyebrow="Resources · Support"
  title="SLA and post-launch support"
  intro="Service levels, response times and support channels once the project is in production."
  description="Siscodex's post-launch service levels and support channels."
  path="/en/recursos/soporte"
  noindex
>
  <h2>Severity levels</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Critical:</strong> service down in production — response within 2 hours.</li>
    <li><strong>High:</strong> degraded functionality without full downtime — response within 8 business hours.</li>
    <li><strong>Normal:</strong> improvements, minor bugs or inquiries — response within 2 business days.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Support channels</h2>
  <p>
    The primary support channel is the same one used during development (Slack or Teams). For
    critical incidents outside business hours, an on-call contact is defined at the start of the
    support agreement.
  </p>
</SimpleContentLayout>
